Helpers that make an OPNsense CARP pair fail over cleanly:

* Keep the kernel default route on a reachable upstream gateway on both
  nodes, and give the backup node internet access through the master.
* Restart Unbound on takeover so the new master does not answer from
  failures it cached as backup.
* Run selected services (UPnP, mDNS relay, ...) on the master only.
* Hand Tailscale subnet routes from the backup to the master.
* Set pfsync maxupd and jumbo MTUs at boot.

A WAN with a single DHCP address on a CARP VIP needs os-carp-vip-dhcp by
Tore Amundsen (BSD-2-Clause, not in the OPNsense repositories), which keeps
the DHCP lease on the CARP VIP so the address fails over with it. Install it
separately; this plugin works with it unmodified.

WWW: https://github.com/kawaconnect/opnsense-ha

